{"parentUuid":"74bae21e-825c-4581-88ab-dd50271d54a1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfkBJxuwjhNVqD2xA9hSv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I think it's a good idea for later. Right now it's probably a distraction, and there's a smaller version worth building first.\n\n**Why it's tempting.** Your repo already behaves like a data model. It has IDs (SQ, P, RQ, O, D, E), rules that never change (never rename an ID), dependencies (sls/5 → dsrm/1, sls/4 → dsrm/3), stop rules (snowballing ends when an iteration finds no new papers) and staleness checks (the \"last synced\" column). Those are things software is good at checking.\n\n**Why I'd hold off on a TUI:**\n- **It's not your thesis.** Your contribution is message semantics down to the hardware. A research-workflow app is a second project, and that's a common way theses stall.\n- **Your process hasn't been used yet.** Most `step.md` files are still templates. Building a UI around a workflow you haven't run once means locking in guesses. Run one full snowballing iteration first, then automate what actually hurt.\n- **Markdown plus git is already a decent interface.** A TUI mostly adds navigation, which your editor already gives you.\n\n**Agents have a specific risk here.** Kitchenham and Charters require that selection and extraction be reproducible and judged by the researcher. Agents fit well for:\n- fetching references and citing papers for each snowballing round\n- drafting first-pass extraction forms for you to correct\n- flagging papers that look relevant to the concept matrix\n\nThey should not make inclusion or exclusion decisions or write the gap. If they help at all, log that in the protocol, because an examiner will ask.\n\n**What I'd build instead, now:** a `just check` command (you already have a `justfile`) backed by a small script that:\n1. checks traceability: every O, D and E names an ID that exists\n2. reports IDs that were renamed or removed instead of retired\n3. marks chapters stale when their source changed after the \"last synced\" commit\n4. checks the snowballing stop rule: did the last iteration add any new P IDs?\n\nThat's a day of work. It enforces the rules you wrote, and it becomes the core of a TUI or agent workflow later if you still want one. Once the thesis is done, the whole tool could also become its own publishable artifact.\n\nWant me to sketch that check script against your current file layout?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71,"cache_read_input_tokens":43267,"output_tokens":988,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":246},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":988,"cache_read_input_tokens":43267,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7e089513-1435-43f8-9263-9be66237566b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfkBJxJjPoyjg3LVx8rCP","type":"assistant","uuid":"38c9d4a6-fd12-4b4f-b54f-6707c5febb96","timestamp":"2026-10-06T02:16:26.272Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
