{"parentUuid":"e8ee52f5-5291-4089-b229-8c172ce379c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfkEM9BjrJXzCEajC1C8e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your argument is stronger now. The step lists show that most of the workflow is mechanical: fill a form, check against criteria, loop until a stop rule. Systematizing that does free you to work on the thesis itself. My objection is to building a separate app. The real cost is the TUI, the state model, the agent orchestration and the tests, and none of that becomes thesis material.\n\n**You already have the app.** Claude Code supports typed agents (`.claude/agents/*.md`, each with its own role and tools), skills (`.claude/skills/`, reusable step procedures) and hooks. Your repo is the state. So the system you're describing is mostly configuration:\n\n| Step | Agent / skill | Does | You decide |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SLS 2 | `snowballer` | Fetches references and citations for the last round's papers, pre-screens them against I/X | Final include/exclude |\n| SLS 3 | `reader` | Drafts the five Cs, Q scores and extraction fields with page numbers | Corrects the record; reads key papers in full yourself |\n| SLS 4 | `synthesizer` | Updates the concept matrix, proposes new concepts | Accepts or merges concepts |\n| SLS 5 / DSRM 1 | `skeptic` | Looks for counter-evidence to H1–H3 and your claims | What to address |\n| DSRM 3–5 | `builder` + `evaluator` | Writes simulator code and tests, runs demos, logs D/E entries | Objectives, metrics, next iteration |\n| DSRM 6 | `drafter` | Turns your outline and claims into chapter prose | Outline, claims, final wording |\n| All | `just check` | Traceability, the ID rule, stale chapters, the stop rule | — |\n\nThe iterative workflows are the loops you already defined. The snowballing loop runs until a round adds no new P IDs. The design loop (3 → 4 → 5) runs until every objective is met or sends you back to step 2. Each agent's output goes into the right `step.md` section, so your AI-usage line and log come for free.\n\n**Cost:** a few days of writing agent definitions, against weeks or months for a custom TUI. And if you outgrow it, these definitions are the spec for a real app later.\n\n**Where I'd start:** SLS is your next real step, so start with `snowballer` + `reader` + `just check`. Running one round will show whether the agent split holds up before you build the rest.\n\nA custom app is worth it only if you want the tool to be a contribution in its own right (for other students, or a paper about it). That's a separate project; plan it after the thesis or with your advisor's blessing.\n\nShould I scaffold the first three: the two agent definitions and the check recipe?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":130,"cache_read_input_tokens":56208,"output_tokens":1238,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":345},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":130,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1238,"cache_read_input_tokens":56208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":130,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":130},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"48885525-2456-4770-869e-eb4ba7b98e98","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfkEM8rt68Rz9hEEjHK3x","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f463c57-1782-43e5-bdea-11d09e6020bc","timestamp":"2026-10-06T02:56:21.295Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis","sessi