{"parentUuid":"d29e2dd2-8caa-4cb0-99c9-ed6bf1ae43a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfkz6aKmw1CZd8hBE3ee8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. It's a better design than what I proposed: your step 1 draft becomes the input that starts the whole pipeline. You already have more to feed it than an observation: a provisional problem, hypotheses H1–H3, RQs and 21 references. The one rule is that the AI can draft everything after your input, but you approve the protocol before any search runs.\n\n**Kickstart flow:**\n\n| # | Who | Input | Output | Gate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | You | — | `dsrm/1` draft (observation, motivation, H1–H3, RQs), marked *provisional* | — |\n| 1a | `protocol-critic` | Step 0 | Draft protocol: SQs derived from your claims and hypotheses, I/X criteria, checklist, extraction form | — |\n| 1b | `skeptic` | Draft protocol | Adds SQs that look for evidence against you (e.g. \"what makes message passing fail?\") | — |\n| 1c | You | Both | Approved protocol | **Protocol frozen.** Later changes go to the 1.6 log. |\n| 2 | `snowballer` | Frozen protocol + your 21 references | Start set: your references **plus** results from a database search string | You approve the start set |\n| 3+ | Normal loop | | | |\n\n**Why the two safeguards matter.** Your draft already argues for a conclusion, so feeding it to the AI carries some of that slant forward:\n- **Protocol drawn only from your hypotheses:** the review would only look for support. The `skeptic` SQs fix that.\n- **Start set drawn only from your references:** snowballing from papers you picked to support your argument mostly finds more of the same. Wohlin recommends a varied start set; the database search string provides it.\n\n**At the end, the loop returns to your input.** At SLS 5, the `synthesizer` compares the gap and answers against your provisional step 1 and lists what's confirmed, what needs revising and what's contradicted. You revise `dsrm/1` and drop the *provisional* label. That gives you a clean record: draft → review → revised problem. It also answers the \"problem before literature\" issue I raised, so your step 1.1 can stay where it is.\n\nShould I write the full table plus this kickstart flow into `research/agents.md`?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1257,"cache_read_input_tokens":61026,"output_tokens":1235,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":486},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1257,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1235,"cache_read_input_tokens":61026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1257,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1257},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2a3ab10b-7b50-425b-86df-e5136a077e56","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfkz6XufqG9pJpmkNqArE","type":"assistant","uuid":"0f375e44-311f-475b-90dd-5f0c59561606","timestamp":"2026-10-06T12:29:56.927Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
