{"parentUuid":"40ce9724-d2c8-4834-b1f6-4537e1ba6973","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfkzW7D34S22tr77yC147","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the full flow. The `#` column shows where each loop starts and ends.\n\n| # | Who | Input | Output | Gate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **0** | You | — | `dsrm/1` draft: observation, motivation, H1–H3, stakeholders, design problem, RQs, marked *provisional* | — |\n| **SLS 1 Protocol** | | | | |\n| 1a | `protocol-critic` | Step 0 | Draft protocol: need for the review, existing reviews, SQs from your claims, I/X criteria, checklist, extraction form | — |\n| 1b | `skeptic` | Draft protocol | SQs looking for counter-evidence | — |\n| 1c | You | 1a + 1b | Approved protocol | **Protocol frozen.** Later changes go to the 1.6 log. |\n| **SLS 2 Search** | | | | |\n| 2a | `snowballer` | Frozen protocol, your references, database search string | Proposed start set, each paper with the I/X criterion it matches | — |\n| 2b | You | 2a | Start set, P IDs assigned | **Include/exclude** |\n| 2c | `snowballer` | Papers included in the last round | Backward + forward candidates, pre-screened | — |\n| 2d | You | 2c | Newly included P IDs | **Include/exclude** |\n| **SLS 3 Reading** (for each new P) | | | | |\n| 3a | `reader` | Paper, protocol 1.4–1.5 | Draft record: five Cs, Q scores, extraction fields, concepts, all with page numbers | — |\n| 3b | `citation-checker` | 3a + paper | Page references verified or flagged | — |\n| 3c | You | 3a + 3b | Corrected record; key papers read in full | **Record accepted** |\n| **SLS 4 Synthesis** | | | | |\n| 4a | `synthesizer` | Accepted records | Proposed concepts, updated matrix, comparison for each concept | — |\n| 4b | You | 4a | Concepts merged/split, comparisons accepted | **Matrix accepted** |\n| ↺ | `just check` | 2d | Did the round add new papers? Yes → **back to 2c**. No → 5a | Stop rule |\n| **SLS 5 Gap** | | | | |\n| 5a | `synthesizer` | Final matrix | Draft SQ answers, gap, current solutions, history, limitations | — |\n| 5b | `skeptic` | 5a | Attacks the gap: is it really uncovered, or just not found? | — |\n| 5c | You | 5a + 5b | Gap stated | **Gap is yours** |\n| **DSRM 1 Problem (revision)** | | | | |\n| 6a | `synthesizer` | SLS 5, step 0 | Diff of step 0: confirmed / to revise / contradicted, claim by claim | — |\n| 6b | `skeptic` | Step 0 + 6a | Attacks motivation, H1–H3, and whether each RQ can be answered \"no\" | — |\n| 6c | You | 6a + 6b | Revised `dsrm/1`, *provisional* removed | **Problem and RQs** |\n| **DSRM 2 Objectives** | | | | |\n| 7a | `skeptic` | RQs, SLS 5, your draft objectives | Each O checked: traces to an RQ, checkable, feasible | — |\n| 7b | You | 7a | Objectives, metrics, baselines for RQ3 | **Objectives frozen** before any results |\n| **DSRM 3 Design** | | | | |\n| 8a | `designer` | Objectives, SLS 4, decisions so far | Options for each open decision, with trade-offs and prior art | — |\n| 8b | You | 8a | Chosen option and reason in the decisions table | **Design choices** |\n| 8c | `builder` | Decisions, current layer | Layer in its form (spec / simulator / formal model / HDL) and its checks | — |\n| 8d | You | 8c | Layer reviewed; you can explain it | **Layer accepted** |\n| **DSRM 4 Demonstration** | | | | |\n| 9a | `demonstrator` | Layer, objectives | Proposed demonstration plan (D IDs, instances) | — |\n| 9b | You | 9a | Plan approved | **Plan** |\n| 9c | `demonstrator` | Plan, layer | Runs or hand traces, D log entries | — |\n| 9d | You | 9c | \"Solved\" confirmed | **Solved?** |\n| **DSRM 5 Evaluation** | | | | |\n| 10a | `evaluator` | Objectives, D log, metrics | Measurements vs baselines, draft E entries, draft threats to validity | — |\n| 10b | `skeptic` | 10a | Attacks baselines, validity, choice of instances | — |\n| 10c | You | 10a + 10b | Met / not met, threats addressed | **Results** |\n| ↺ | You | 10c | Next layer or fix → **8a**. Objective wrong → **7a**. All objectives met → 11a. | **Iteration** |\n| **DSRM 6 Communicate** | | | | |\n| 11a | You | Stable steps | Outline + key claims for each chapter | **Argument is yours** |\n| 11b | `drafter` | 11a + sources | Chapter prose | — |\n| 11c | `citation-checker` | 11b | Each cited claim verified against its source | — |\n| 11d | `examiner` | 11b | Questions your defense committee would ask | — |\n| 11e | You | 11b–11d | Final wording, contribution type, answers to the questions | **Text is yours** |\n| ↺ | You | 11d–11e | Writing exposes a hole → **7a** or **8a** | **Iteration** |\n\n**Throughout:**\n- `just check` runs after every gate: traceability, the ID rule, stale chapters.\n- Every agent step appends to the AI log: agent, step, proposal, and whether you accepted, changed or rejected it.\n\nThat's 22 gates for you, and every one is a decision rather than a piece of work. Should I put this table into `research/agents.md` next?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46,"cache_read_input_tokens":63518,"output_tokens":2174,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":95},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2174,"cache_read_input_tokens":63518,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"817e9237-bf1c-4648-873b-2ba4f2c49eeb","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfkzW6PgUXXnQ7o5k5E4m","type":"assistant","uuid":"e7ac29df-c4f7-46a1-8349-587214471f8c","timestamp":"2026-10-06T12:35:20.315Z","advisorModel":"claude