oy / Coq model | Model checker or proof |\n| 4. Hardware prototype | HDL (Verilog / VHDL / Chisel), FPGA build | HDL simulation, synthesis reports, board runs |\n\nBesides the layers themselves, the builder also produces benchmark programs, the toolchain (assembler, language front end) and figures.\n\n## Kickstart\nThe pipeline starts from my provisional draft (step 0). Two safeguards, because that draft already argues for a conclusion:\n- **Protocol bias:** SQs drawn only from my hypotheses would only look for support. `skeptic` adds SQs that look for evidence against them (1b).\n- **Start set bias:** snowballing only from my own references mostly finds more of the same. The start set also uses a database search string (2a), as Wohlin recommends a varied start set [1].\n\nAt the end of the SLS, the loop returns to step 0: the `synthesizer` lists which claims are confirmed, need revising or are contradicted (6a), and I revise the draft before removing the *provisional* label.\n\n## Flow (problem-centred route)\n`↺` rows are loop decisions.\n\n| # | Who | Input | Output | Gate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **0** | Me | — | `dsrm/1` draft: observation, motivation, H1–H3, stakeholders, design problem, RQs, marked *provisional* | — |\n| **SLS 1 Protocol** · `sls-1-protocol` | | | | |\n| 1a | `protocol-critic` | Step 0 | Draft protocol: need for the review, existing reviews, SQs from my claims, I/X criteria, checklist, extraction form | — |\n| 1b | `skeptic` | Draft protocol | SQs looking for counter-evidence | — |\n| 1c | Me | 1a + 1b | Approved protocol | **Protocol frozen.** Later changes go to the 1.6 log. |\n| **SLS 2 Search** · `sls-2-search` | | | | |\n| 2a | `snowballer` | Frozen protocol, my references, database search string | Proposed start set, each paper with the I/X criterion it matches | — |\n| 2b | Me | 2a | Start set, P IDs assigned | **Include/exclude** |\n| 2c | `snowballer` | Papers included in the last round | Backward and forward candidates, pre-screened | — |\n| 2d | Me | 2c | Newly included P IDs | **Include/exclude** |\n| **SLS 3 Reading** · `sls-3-reading` (for each new P) | | | | |\n| 3a | `reader` | Paper, protocol 1.4–1.5 | Draft record: five Cs, Q scores, extraction fields, concepts, all with pages | — |\n| 3b | `citation-checker` | 3a + paper | Page references verified or flagged | — |\n| 3c | Me | 3a + 3b | Corrected record; key papers read in full | **Record accepted** |\n| **SLS 4 Synthesis** · `sls-4-synthesis` | | | | |\n| 4a | `synthesizer` | Accepted records | Proposed concepts, updated matrix, comparison for each concept | — |\n| 4b | Me | 4a | Concepts merged or split, comparisons accepted | **Matrix accepted** |\n| ↺ | `just check` | 2d | Did the round add new papers? Yes → back to 2c. No → 5a | Stop rule [1] |\n| **SLS 5 Gap** · `sls-5-gap` | | | | |\n| 5a | `synthesizer` | Final matrix | Draft SQ answers, gap, current solutions, history, limitations | — |\n| 5b | `skeptic` | 5a | Attacks the gap: really uncovered, or just not found? | — |\n| 5c | Me | 5a + 5b | Gap stated | **Gap** |\n| **DSRM 1 Problem (revision)** · `dsrm-1-problem` | | | | |\n| 6a | `synthesizer` | SLS 5, step 0 | Diff of step 0, claim by claim: confirmed / to revise / contradicted | — |\n| 6b | `skeptic` | Step 0 + 6a | Attacks motivation, H1–H3, and whether each RQ can be answered \"no\" | — |\n| 6c | Me | 6a + 6b | Revised `dsrm/1`, *provisional* removed | **Problem and RQs** |\n| **DSRM 2 Objectives** · `dsrm-2-objectives` | | | | |\n| 7a | `skeptic` | RQs, SLS 5, my draft objectives | Each O checked: traces to an RQ, checkable, feasible | — |\n| 7b | Me | 7a | Objectives, metrics, baselines for RQ3 | **Objectives frozen** before any results |\n| **DSRM 3 Design** · `dsrm-3-design` | | | | |\n| 8a | `designer` | Objectives, SLS 4, decisions so far | Options for each open decision, with trade-offs and prior art | — |\n| 8b | Me | 8a | Chosen option and reason, in the decisions table | **Design choices** |\n| 8c | `builder` | Decisions, current layer | Layer in its form and its checks | — |\n| 8d | Me | 8c | Layer reviewed; I can explain it | **Layer accepted** |\n| **DSRM 4 Demonstration** · `dsrm-4-demonstration` | | | | |\n| 9a | `demonstrator` | Layer, objectives | Proposed demonstration plan (D IDs, instances) | — |\n| 9b | Me | 9a | Plan approved | **Plan** |\n| 9c | `demonstrator` | Plan, layer | Runs or hand traces, D log entries | — |\n| 9d | Me | 9c | \"Solved\" confirmed | **Solved?** |\n| **DSRM 5 Evaluation** · `dsrm-5-evaluation` | | | | |\n| 10a | `evaluator` | Objectives, D log, metrics | Measurements against baselines, draft E entries, draft threats to validity | — |\n| 10b | `skeptic` | 10a | Attacks baselines, validity, choice of instances | — |\n| 10c | Me | 10a + 10b | Met / not met, threats addressed | **Results** |\n| ↺ | Me | 10c | Next layer or fix → 8a. Objective wrong → 7a. All objectives met → 11a | **Iteration** [2] |\n| **DSRM 6 Communicate** · `dsrm-6-communicate` | | | | |\n| 11a | Me | Stable steps | Outline and key claims for each chapter | **Argument** |\n| 11b | `drafter` | 11a + sources | Chapter prose | — |\n| 11c | `citation-checker` | 11b | Each cited claim verified against its source | — |\n| 11d | `examiner` | 11b | Questions the committee would ask | — |\n| 11e | Me | 11b–11d | Final wording, contribution type, answers to the questions | **Text** |\n| ↺ | Me | 11d–11e | Writing exposes a hole → 7a or 8a | **Iteration** [2] |\n\n## AI log\nEverything the AI does is recorded, not only the decisions. Two parts in `research/ai-log/`:\n\n**1. Raw log** (`raw/<session>.jsonl`): every action, written automatically.\n- Written by Claude Code hooks, not by the agents, so no agent can forget or leave out an entry.\n- One entry per event: my prompts, skill calls, agent starts and stops, and every tool call with its full input and full output.\n- Each entry records: timestamp, session, skill, agent, flow row (e.g. `3a`), event type, input, output.\n- At session end, the session transcript is copied in as well. It also holds the model's own messages, which tool hooks do not see.\n- Append only. Never edited by hand.\n\n**2. Decision log** (`decisions.md`): one entry per gate.\n```\nDate:\nRow: 3c\nProposed by: reader, citation-checker\nProposal:\nDecision: accepted / changed / rejected\nWhat I changed and why:\nRaw log entries: <session> <first>–<last>\n```\n\nThe raw log shows what the AI did. The decision log shows what I did with it. Each decision points to the raw entries behind it.\n\n## Throughout\n- **`just check`** runs after every gate: traceability, the ID rule, stale chapters, and that every gate has a decision log entry.\n- **AI log:** see above.\n\n---\n\n## References\n1. Wohlin (2014). *Guidelines for Snowballing in Systematic Literature Studies*. Conference on Evaluation and Assessment in Software Engineering.\n2. Peffers et al. (2007). *A Design Science Research Methodology for Information Systems Research*. Journal of Management Information Systems 24(3).\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1bb84217-7cb0-406d-a31d-71334b4f2a87","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfm2UrANWBKPFbUSDqVbg","type":"assistant","uuid":"b4aeb553-b9c8-4d8f-a6b8-d094d3c6e193","timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:01:57.377Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b4aeb553-b9c8-4d8f-a6b8-d094d3c6e193","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b351a258-fb0e-4307-98f3-5b2bc3606b83","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UbFHywyFdfHJPp8c34ds5N","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/agents.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b1a6ac48-6dde-4d53-8fb2-bb88bd4c0114","timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:01:57.524Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/agents.md","content":"# AI agents and workflow\n\nHow AI skills and agents run the steps of `sls/` and `dsrm/`. These are working rules. They do not change either method.\n\n## The line\n- **AI does the labour:** searching, drafting, building, measuring, writing prose.\n- **I make the decisions:** every row marked as a gate below. Each one is a decision, not a piece of work.\n- **Test:** I can defend every output at the defense with no AI in the room.\n- **Everything is logged:** every action the AI takes, not only the decisions (see *AI log*). The thesis Method chapter states how AI was used.\n\n## Skills\nThree levels of facades. Every skill can be called on its own.\n\n```\nthesis                      entry point → route through sls and dsrm\n├── sls                     runs SLS 1 → 5, with the snowballing loop\n│   ├── sls-1-protocol\n│   ├── sls-2-search\n│   ├── sls-3-reading\n│   ├── sls-4-synthesis\n│   └── sls-5-gap\n└── dsrm                    runs DSRM 1 → 6, with the design loop\n    ├── dsrm-1-problem\n    ├── dsrm-2-objectives\n    ├── dsrm-3-design\n    ├── dsrm-4-demonstration\n    ├── dsrm-5-evaluation\n    └── dsrm-6-communicate\n```\n\n- **`thesis`** asks for the entry point (see *Entry points*) and calls `sls` and `dsrm` in the order that entry point needs.\n- **`sls`** and **`dsrm`** run their steps in order, handle their loops, and stop at every gate.\n- **Step skills** run the rows of the *Flow* table for their step: they call the agents, then stop at the gate. Called directly, they work on the current state of their `step.md` (e.g. `sls-3-reading P12` reads one paper).\n- **Skills are procedures, agents are workers.** Step skills call agents; agents never call skills.\n\n## Entry points\nPeffers et al. define four entry points [2]. The DSRM sequence is the same in all four; only the starting activity changes.\n\n| Entry point [2] | Starts at | Trigger | Route |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Problem-centred initiation | DSRM 1 | An observed problem | Step 0 (my `dsrm/1` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 revised → 2 → 3–5 loop → 6. **This thesis.** The *Flow* table below is this route. |\n| Objective-centred solution | DSRM 2 | A need that a better artifact could meet | Step 0 (my `dsrm/2` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 written, 2 revised → 3–5 loop → 6 |\n| Design and development-centred initiation | DSRM 3 | An existing artifact not yet thought through as a solution to this problem | Step 0 (the artifact, described in `dsrm/3`) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1–2 written for the problem it solves → 3–5 loop → 6 |\n| Client/context initiated | DSRM 4 | A practical solution observed to work | Step 0 (the observed solution, in `dsrm/4`) → SLS 1–5 → work backward through DSRM 3, 2, 1 to apply rigor retroactively [2] → 5 → 6 |\n\nMy rules for all four (not part of Peffers):\n- Step 0 is always my draft of the starting activity, marked *provisional*.\n- The SLS always runs right after step 0, because DSRM 1–3 need it (`research/README.md`).\n- The kickstart safeguards apply whatever the entry point.\n\n## Agents\n| Agent | Used in | Does |\n|---|---|---|\n| `protocol-critic` | SLS 1 | Drafts the protocol from step 0; checks that SQs are answerable, criteria can be applied without ambiguity, and the form covers every SQ |\n| `snowballer` | SLS 2 | Proposes the start set; fetches backward and forward candidates; pre-screens each against I/X |\n| `reader` | SLS 3 | Drafts the record for each paper: five Cs, Q scores, extraction fields, concepts, with pages |\n| `synthesizer` | SLS 4, SLS 5, DSRM 1 | Proposes concepts and the matrix; drafts SQ answers and gap; compares SLS 5 against step 0 |\n| `designer` | DSRM 3 | For each open decision: options, trade-offs against objectives and prior art; critiques my proposals |\n| `builder` | DSRM 3 | Produces the current layer in its form (see *Builder output per layer*) |\n| `demonstrator` | DSRM 4 | Proposes the demonstration plan; writes problem instances; runs or traces them; logs D entries |\n| `evaluator` | DSRM 5 | Measures against baselines; drafts E entries and threats to validity |\n| `drafter` | DSRM 6 | Turns my outline and claims into chapter prose |\n| `examiner` | DSRM 6 | Plays the committee: asks the questions I will face at the defense |\n| `skeptic` | Any step | Looks for counter-evidence and attacks claims, gaps, objectives and results |\n| `citation-checker` | Any step | Checks that each cited claim appears in the source at the cited page |\n\n## Builder output per layer\nLayers from `dsrm/3-design/step.md`.\n\n| Layer | Form | Check |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Paper design | Spec document: instruction set, message format, actor lifecycle, diagrams | Consistency review, worked traces by hand |\n| 2. Executable model / simulator | Code and tests | Test suite, actor programs run end to end |\n| 3. Formal specification | TLA+ / Alloy / Coq model | Model checker or proof |\n| 4. Hardware prototype | HDL (Verilog / VHDL / Chisel), FPGA build | HDL simulation, synthesis reports, board runs |\n\nBesides the layers themselves, the builder also produces benchmark programs, the toolchain (assembler, language front end) and figures.\n\n## Kickstart\nThe pipeline starts from my provisional draft (step 0). Two safeguards, because that draft already argues for a conclusion:\n- **Protocol bias:** SQs drawn only from my hypotheses would only look for support. `skeptic` adds SQs that look for evidence against them (1b).\n- **Start set bias:** snowballing only from my own references mostly finds more of the same. The start set also uses a database search string (2a), as Wohlin recommends a varied start set [1].\n\nAt the end of the SLS, the loop returns to step 0: the `synthesizer` lists which claims are confirmed, need revising or are contradicted (6a), and I revise the draft before removing the *provisional* label.\n\n## Flow (problem-centred route)\n`↺` rows are loop decisions.\n\n| # | Who | Input | Output | Gate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **0** | Me | — | `dsrm/1` draft: observation, motivation, H1–H3, stakeholders, design problem, RQs, marked *provisional* | — |\n| **SLS 1 Protocol** · `sls-1-protocol` | | | | |\n| 1a | `protocol-critic` | Step 0 | Draft protocol: need for the review, existing reviews, SQs from my claims, I/X criteria, checklist, extraction form | — |\n| 1b | `skeptic` | Draft protocol | SQs looking for counter-evidence | — |\n| 1c | Me | 1a + 1b | Approved protocol | **Protocol frozen.** Later changes go to the 1.6 log. |\n| **SLS 2 Search** · `sls-2-search` | | | | |\n| 2a | `snowballer` | Frozen protocol, my references, database search string | Proposed start set, each paper with the I/X criterion it matches | — |\n| 2b | Me | 2a | Start set, P IDs assigned | **Include/exclude** |\n| 2c | `snowballer` | Papers included in the last round | Backward and forward candidates, pre-screened | — |\n| 2d | Me | 2c | Newly included P IDs | **Include/exclude** |\n| **SLS 3 Reading** · `sls-3-reading` (for each new P) | | | | |\n| 3a | `reader` | Paper, protocol 1.4–1.5 | Draft record: five Cs, Q scores, extraction fields, concepts, all with pages | — |\n| 3b | `citation-checker` | 3a + paper | Page references verified or flagged | — |\n| 3c | Me | 3a + 3b | Corrected record; key papers read in full | **Record accepted** |\n| **SLS 4 Synthesis** · `sls-4-synthesis` | | | | |\n| 4a | `synthesizer` | Accepted records | Proposed concepts, updated matrix, comparison for each concept | — |\n| 4b | Me | 4a | Concepts merged or split, comparisons accepted | **Matrix accepted** |\n| ↺ | `just check` | 2d | Did the round add new papers? Yes → back to 2c. No → 5a | Stop rule [1] |\n| **SLS 5 Gap** · `sls-5-gap` | | | | |\n| 5a | `synthesizer` | Final matrix | Draft SQ answers, gap, current solutions, history, limitations | — |\n| 5b | `skeptic` | 5a | Attacks the gap: really uncovered, or just not found? | — |\n| 5c | Me | 5a + 5b | Gap stated | **Gap** |\n| **DSRM 1 Problem (revision)** · `dsrm-1-problem` | | | | |\n| 6a | `synthesizer` | SLS 5, step 0 | Diff of step 0, claim by claim: confirmed / to revise / contradicted | — |\n| 6b | `skeptic` | Step 0 + 6a | Attacks motivation, H1–H3, and whether each RQ can be answered \"no\" | — |\n| 6c | Me | 6a + 6b | Revised `dsrm/1`, *provisional* removed | **Problem and RQs** |\n| **DSRM 2 Objectives** · `dsrm-2-objectives` | | | | |\n| 7a | `skeptic` | RQs, SLS 5, my draft objectives | Each O checked: traces to an RQ, checkable, feasible | — |\n| 7b | Me | 7a | Objectives, metrics, baselines for RQ3 | **Objectives frozen** before any results |\n| **DSRM 3 Design** · `dsrm-3-design` | | | | |\n| 8a | `designer` | Objectives, SLS 4, decisions so far | Options for each open decision, with trade-offs and prior art | — |\n| 8b | Me | 8a | Chosen option and reason, in the decisions table | **Design choices** |\n| 8c | `builder` | Decisions, current layer | Layer in its form and its checks | — |\n| 8d | Me | 8c | Layer reviewed; I can explain it | **Layer accepted** |\n| **DSRM 4 Demonstration** · `dsrm-4-demonstration` | | | | |\n| 9a | `demonstrator` | Layer, objectives | Proposed demonstration plan (D IDs, instances) | — |\n| 9b | Me | 9a | Plan approved | **Plan** |\n| 9c | `demonstrator` | Plan, layer | Runs or hand traces, D log entries | — |\n| 9d | Me | 9c | \"Solved\" confirmed | **Solved?** |\n| **DSRM 5 Evaluation** · `dsrm-5-evaluation` | | | | |\n| 10a | `evaluator` | Objectives, D log, metrics | Measurements against baselines, draft E entries, draft threats to validity | — |\n| 10b | `skeptic` | 10a | Attacks baselines, validity, choice of instances | — |\n| 10c | Me | 10a + 10b | Met / not met, threats addressed | **Results** |\n| ↺ | Me | 10c | Next layer or fix → 8a. Objective wrong → 7a. All objectives met → 11a | **Iteration** [2] |\n| **DSRM 6 Communicate** · `dsrm-6-communicate` | | | | |\n| 11a | Me | Stable steps | Outline and key claims for each chapter | **Argument** |\n| 11b | `drafter` | 11a + sources | Chapter prose | — |\n| 11c | `citation-checker` | 11b | Each cited claim verified against its source | — |\n| 11d | `examiner` | 11b | Questions the committee would ask | — |\n| 11e | Me | 11b–11d | Final wording, contribution type, answers to the questions | **Text** |\n| ↺ | Me | 11d–11e | Writing exposes a hole → 7a or 8a | **Iteration** [2] |\n\n## AI log\nEverything the AI does is recorded, not only the decisions. Two parts in `research/ai-log/`:\n\n**1. Raw log** (`raw/<session>.jsonl`): every action, written automatically.\n- Written by Claude Code hooks, not by the agents, so no agent can forget or leave out an entry.\n- One entry per event: my prompts, skill calls, agent starts and stops, and every tool call with its full input and full output.\n- Each entry records: timestamp, session, skill, agent, flow row (e.g. `3a`), event type, input, output.\n- At session end, the session transcript is copied in as well. It also holds the model's own messages, which tool hooks do not see.\n- Append only. Never edited by hand.\n\n**2. Decision log** (`decisions.md`): one entry per gate.\n```\nDate:\nRow: 3c\nProposed by: reader, citation-checker\nProposal:\nDecision: accepted / changed / rejected\nWhat I changed and why:\nRaw log entries: <session> <first>–<last>\n```\n\nThe raw log shows what the AI did. The decision log shows what I did with it. Each decision points to the raw entries behind it.\n\n## Throughout\n- **`just check`** runs after every gate: traceability, the ID rule, stale chapters, and that every gate has a decision log entry.\n- **AI log:** see above.\n\n---\n\n## References\n1. Wohlin (2014). *Guidelines for Snowballing in Systematic Literature Studies*. Conference on Evaluation and Assessment in Software Engineering.\n2. Peffers et al. (2007). *A Design Science Research Methodology for Information Systems Research*. Journal of Management Information Systems 24(3).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":13,"newStart":1,"newLines":53,"lines":[" # AI agents and workflow"," ","-How AI agents run the steps of `sls/` and `dsrm/`. These are working rules. They do not change either method.","+How AI skills and agents run the steps of `sls/` and `dsrm/`. These are working rules. They do not change either method."," "," ## The line"," - **AI does the labour:** searching, drafting, building, measuring, writing prose."," - **I make the decisions:** every row marked as a gate below. Each one is a decision, not a piece of work."," - **Test:** I can defend every output at the defense with no AI in the room.","-- **Disclosure:** every agent run is logged (see *Throughout*), and the thesis Method chapter states how AI was used.","+- **Everything is logged:** every action the AI takes, not only the decisions (see *AI log*). The thesis Method chapter states how AI was used."," ","+## Skills","+Three levels of facades. Every skill can be called on its own.","+","+```","+thesis                      entry point → route through sls and dsrm","+├── sls                     runs SLS 1 → 5, with the snowballing loop","+│   ├── sls-1-protocol","+│   ├── sls-2-search","+│   ├── sls-3-reading","+│   ├── sls-4-synthesis","+│   └── sls-5-gap","+└── dsrm                    runs DSRM 1 → 6, with the design loop","+    ├── dsrm-1-problem","+    ├── dsrm-2-objectives","+    ├── dsrm-3-design","+    ├── dsrm-4-demonstration","+    ├── dsrm-5-evaluation","+    └── dsrm-6-communicate","+```","+","+- **`thesis`** asks for the entry point (see *Entry points*) and calls `sls` and `dsrm` in the order that entry point needs.","+- **`sls`** and **`dsrm`** run their steps in order, handle their loops, and stop at every gate.","+- **Step skills** run the rows of the *Flow* table for their step: they call the agents, then stop at the gate. Called directly, they work on the current state of their `step.md` (e.g. `sls-3-reading P12` reads one paper).","+- **Skills are procedures, agents are workers.** Step skills call agents; agents never call skills.","+","+## Entry points","+Peffers et al. define four entry points [2]. The DSRM sequence is the same in all four; only the starting activity changes.","+","+| Entry point [2] | Starts at | Trigger | Route |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| Problem-centred initiation | DSRM 1 | An observed problem | Step 0 (my `dsrm/1` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 revised → 2 → 3–5 loop → 6. **This thesis.** The *Flow* table below is this route. |","+| Objective-centred solution | DSRM 2 | A need that a better artifact could meet | Step 0 (my `dsrm/2` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 written, 2 revised → 3–5 loop → 6 |","+| Design and development-centred initiation | DSRM 3 | An existing artifact not yet thought through as a solution to this problem | Step 0 (the artifact, described in `dsrm/3`) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1–2 written for the problem it solves → 3–5 loop → 6 |","+| Client/context initiated | DSRM 4 | A practical solution observed to work | Step 0 (the observed solution, in `dsrm/4`) → SLS 1–5 → work backward through DSRM 3, 2, 1 to apply rigor retroactively [2] → 5 → 6 |","+","+My rules for all four (not part of Peffers):","+- Step 0 is always my draft of the starting activity, marked *provisional*.","+- The SLS always runs right after step 0, because DSRM 1–3 need it (`research/README.md`).","+- The kickstart safeguards apply whatever the entry point.","+"," ## Agents"," | Agent | Used in | Does |"," |---|---|---|"]},{"oldStart":37,"oldLines":62,"newStart":77,"newLines":62,"lines":[" Besides the layers themselves, the builder also produces benchmark programs, the toolchain (assembler, language front end) and figures."," "," ## Kickstart","-The pipeline starts from my provisional `dsrm/1-problem/step.md` (step 0). Two safeguards, because that draft already argues for a conclusion:","+The pipeline starts from my provisional draft (step 0). Two safeguards, because that draft already argues for a conclusion:"," - **Protocol bias:** SQs drawn only from my hypotheses would only look for support. `skeptic` adds SQs that look for evidence against them (1b)."," - **Start set bias:** snowballing only from my own references mostly finds more of the same. The start set also uses a database search string (2a), as Wohlin recommends a varied start set [1]."," ","-At the end of the SLS, the loop returns to step 0: the `synthesizer` lists which claims are confirmed, need revising or are contradicted (6a), and I revise `dsrm/1` before removing the *provisional* label.","+At the end of the SLS, the loop returns to step 0: the `synthesizer` lists which claims are confirmed, need revising or are contradicted (6a), and I revise the draft before removing the *provisional* label."," ","-## Flow","+## Flow (problem-centred route)"," `↺` rows are loop decisions."," "," | # | Who | Input | Output | Gate |"," |---|---|---|---|---|"," | **0** | Me | — | `dsrm/1` draft: observation, motivation, H1–H3, stakeholders, design problem, RQs, marked *provisional* | — |","-| **SLS 1 Protocol** | | | | |","+| **SLS 1 Protocol** · `sls-1-protocol` | | | | |"," | 1a | `protocol-critic` | Step 0 | Draft protocol: need for the review, existing reviews, SQs from my claims, I/X criteria, checklist, extraction form | — |"," | 1b | `skeptic` | Draft protocol | SQs looking for counter-evidence | — |"," | 1c | Me | 1a + 1b | Approved protocol | **Protocol frozen.** Later changes go to the 1.6 log. |","-| **SLS 2 Search** | | | | |","+| **SLS 2 Search** · `sls-2-search` | | | | |"," | 2a | `snowballer` | Frozen protocol, my references, database search string | Proposed start set, each paper with the I/X criterion it matches | — |"," | 2b | Me | 2a | Start set, P IDs assigned | **Include/exclude** |"," | 2c | `snowballer` | Papers included in the last round | Backward and forward candidates, pre-screened | — |"," | 2d | Me | 2c | Newly included P IDs | **Include/exclude** |","-| **SLS 3 Reading** (for each new P) | | | | |","+| **SLS 3 Reading** · `sls-3-reading` (for each new P) | | | | |"," | 3a | `reader` | Paper, protocol 1.4–1.5 | Draft record: five Cs, Q scores, extraction fields, concepts, all with pages | — |"," | 3b | `citation-checker` | 3a + paper | Page references verified or flagged | — |"," | 3c | Me | 3a + 3b | Corrected record; key papers read in full | **Record accepted** |","-| **SLS 4 Synthesis** | | | | |","+| **SLS 4 Synthesis** · `sls-4-synthesis` | | | | |"," | 4a | `synthesizer` | Accepted records | Proposed concepts, updated matrix, comparison for each concept | — |"," | 4b | Me | 4a | Concepts merged or split, comparisons accepted | **Matrix accepted** |"," | ↺ | `just check` | 2d | Did the round add new papers? Yes → back to 2c. No → 5a | Stop rule [1] |","-| **SLS 5 Gap** | | | | |","+| **SLS 5 Gap** · `sls-5-gap` | | | | |"," | 5a | `synthesizer` | Final matrix | Draft SQ answers, gap, current solutions, history, limitations | — |"," | 5b | `skeptic` | 5a | Attacks the gap: really uncovered, or just not found? | — |"," | 5c | Me | 5a + 5b | Gap stated | **Gap** |","-| **DSRM 1 Problem (revision)** | | | | |","+| **DSRM 1 Problem (revision)** · `dsrm-1-problem` | | | | |"," | 6a | `synthesizer` | SLS 5, step 0 | Diff of step 0, claim by claim: confirmed / to revise / contradicted | — |"," | 6b | `skeptic` | Step 0 + 6a | Attacks motivation, H1–H3, and whether each RQ can be answered \"no\" | — |"," | 6c | Me | 6a + 6b | Revised `dsrm/1`, *provisional* removed | **Problem and RQs** |","-| **DSRM 2 Objectives** | | | | |","+| **DSRM 2 Objectives** · `dsrm-2-objectives` | | | | |"," | 7a | `skeptic` | RQs, SLS 5, my draft objectives | Each O checked: traces to an RQ, checkable, feasible | — |"," | 7b | Me | 7a | Objectives, metrics, baselines for RQ3 | **Objectives frozen** before any results |","-| **DSRM 3 Design** | | | | |","+| **DSRM 3 Design** · `dsrm-3-design` | | | | |"," | 8a | `designer` | Objectives, SLS 4, decisions so far | Options for each open decision, with trade-offs and prior art | — |"," | 8b | Me | 8a | Chosen option and reason, in the decisions table | **Design choices** |"," | 8c | `builder` | Decisions, current layer | Layer in its form and its checks | — |"," | 8d | Me | 8c | Layer reviewed; I can explain it | **Layer accepted** |","-| **DSRM 4 Demonstration** | | | | |","+| **DSRM 4 Demonstration** · `dsrm-4-demonstration` | | | | |"," | 9a | `demonstrator` | Layer, objectives | Proposed demonstration plan (D IDs, instances) | — |"," | 9b | Me | 9a | Plan approved | **Plan** |"," | 9c | `demonstrator` | Plan, layer | Runs or hand traces, D log entries | — |"," | 9d | Me | 9c | \"Solved\" confirmed | **Solved?** |","-| **DSRM 5 Evaluation** | | | | |","+| **DSRM 5 Evaluation** · `dsrm-5-evaluation` | | | | |"," | 10a | `evaluator` | Objectives, D log, metrics | Measurements against baselines, draft E entries, draft threats to validity | — |"," | 10b | `skeptic` | 10a | Attacks baselines, validity, choice of instances | — |"," | 10c | Me | 10a + 10b | Met / not met, threats addressed | **Results** |"," | ↺ | Me | 10c | Next layer or fix → 8a. Objective wrong → 7a. All objectives met → 11a | **Iteration** [2] |","-| **DSRM 6 Communicate** | | | | |","+| **DSRM 6 Communicate** · `dsrm-6-communicate` | | | | |"," | 11a | Me | Stable steps | Outline and key claims for each chapter | **Argument** |"," | 11b | `drafter` | 11a + sources | Chapter prose | — |"," | 11c | `citation-checker` | 11b | Each cited claim verified against its source | — |"]},{"oldStart":100,"oldLines":9,"newStart":140,"newLines":32,"lines":[" | 11e | Me | 11b–11d | Final wording, contribution type, answers to the questions | **Text** |"," | ↺ | Me | 11d–11e | Writing exposes a hole → 7a or 8a | **Iteration** [2] |"," ","+## AI log","+Everything the AI does is recorded, not only the decisions. Two parts in `research/ai-log/`:","+","+**1. Raw log** (`raw/<session>.jsonl`): every action, written automatically.","+- Written by Claude Code hooks, not by the agents, so no agent can forget or leave out an entry.","+- One entry per event: my prompts, skill calls, agent starts and stops, and every tool call with its full input and full output.","+- Each entry records: timestamp, session, skill, agent, flow row (e.g. `3a`), event type, input, output.","+- At session end, the session transcript is copied in as well. It also holds the model's own messages, which tool hooks do not see.","+- Append only. Never edited by hand.","+","+**2. Decision log** (`decisions.md`): one entry per gate.","+```","+Date:","+Row: 3c","+Proposed by: reader, citation-checker","+Proposal:","+Decision: accepted / changed / rejected","+What I changed and why:","+Raw log entries: <session> <first>–<last>","+```","+","+The raw log shows what the AI did. The decision log shows what I did with it. Each decision points to the raw entries behind it.","+"," ## Throughout","-- **`just check`** runs after every gate: traceability, the ID rule, stale chapters.","-- **AI log:** every agent step appends agent, step, what it proposed, and whether I accepted, changed or rejected it.","+- **`just check`** runs after every gate: traceability, the ID rule, stale chapters, and that every gate has a decision log entry.","+- **AI log:** see above."," "," ---"," "]}],"originalFile":"# AI agents and workflow\n\nHow AI agents run the steps of `sls/` and `dsrm/`. These are working rules. They do not change either method.\n\n## The line\n- **AI does the labour:** searching, drafting, building, measuring, writing prose.\n- **I make the decisions:** every row marked as a gate below. Each one is a decision, not a piece of work.\n- **Test:** I can defend every output at the defense with no AI in the room.\n- **Disclosure:** every agent run is logged (see *Throughout*), and the thesis Method chapter states how AI was used.\n\n## Agents\n| Agent | Used in | Does |\n|---|---|---|\n| `protocol-critic` | SLS 1 | Drafts the protocol from step 0; checks that SQs are answerable, criteria can be applied without ambiguity, and the form covers every SQ |\n| `snowballer` | SLS 2 | Proposes the start set; fetches backward and forward candidates; pre-screens each against I/X |\n| `reader` | SLS 3 | Drafts the record for each paper: five Cs, Q scores, extraction fields, concepts, with pages |\n| `synthesizer` | SLS 4, SLS 5, DSRM 1 | Proposes concepts and the matrix; drafts SQ answers and gap; compares SLS 5 against step 0 |\n| `designer` | DSRM 3 | For each open decision: options, trade-offs against objectives and prior art; critiques my proposals |\n| `builder` | DSRM 3 | Produces the current layer in its form (see *Builder output per layer*) |\n| `demonstrator` | DSRM 4 | Proposes the demonstration plan; writes problem instances; runs or traces them; logs D entries |\n| `evaluator` | DSRM 5 | Measures against baselines; drafts E entries and threats to validity |\n| `drafter` | DSRM 6 | Turns my outline and claims into chapter prose |\n| `examiner` | DSRM 6 | Plays the committee: asks the questions I will face at the defense |\n| `skeptic` | Any step | Looks for counter-evidence and attacks claims, gaps, objectives and results |\n| `citation-checker` | Any step | Checks that each cited claim appears in the source at the cited page |\n\n## Builder output per layer\nLayers from `dsrm/3-design/step.md`.\n\n| Layer | Form | Check |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Paper design | Spec document: instruction set, message format, actor lifecycle, diagrams | Consistency review, worked traces by hand |\n| 2. Executable model / simulator | Code and tests | Test suite, actor programs run end to end |\n| 3. Formal specification | TLA+ / Alloy / Coq model | Model checker or proof |\n| 4. Hardware prototype | HDL (Verilog / VHDL / Chisel), FPGA build | HDL simulation, synthesis reports, board runs |\n\nBesides the layers themselves, the builder also produces benchmark programs, the toolchain (assembler, language front end) and figures.\n\n## Kickstart\nThe pipeline starts from my provisional `dsrm/1-problem/step.md` (step 0). Two safeguards, because that draft already argues for a conclusion:\n- **Protocol bias:** SQs drawn only from my hypotheses would only look for support. `skeptic` adds SQs that look for evidence against them (1b).\n- **Start set bias:** snowballing only from my own references mostly finds more of the same. The start set also uses a database search string (2a), as Wohlin recommends a varied start set [1].\n\nAt the end of the SLS, the loop returns to step 0: the `synthesizer` lists which claims are confirmed, need revising or are contradicted (6a), and I revise `dsrm/1` before removing the *provisional* label.\n\n## Flow\n`↺` rows are loop decisions.\n\n| # | Who | Input | Output | Gate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **0** | Me | — | `dsrm/1` draft: observation, motivation, H1–H3, stakeholders, design problem, RQs, marked *provisional* | — |\n| **SLS 1 Protocol** | | | | |\n| 1a | `protocol-critic` | Step 0 | Draft protocol: need for the review, existing reviews, SQs from my claims, I/X criteria, checklist, extraction form | — |\n| 1b | `skeptic` | Draft protocol | SQs looking for counter-evidence | — |\n| 1c | Me | 1a + 1b | Approved protocol | **Protocol frozen.** Later changes go to the 1.6 log. |\n| **SLS 2 Search** | | | | |\n| 2a | `snowballer` | Frozen protocol, my references, database search string | Proposed start set, each paper with the I/X criterion it matches | — |\n| 2b | Me | 2a | Start set, P IDs assigned | **Include/exclude** |\n| 2c | `snowballer` | Papers included in the last round | Backward and forward candidates, pre-screened | — |\n| 2d | Me | 2c | Newly included P IDs | **Include/exclude** |\n| **SLS 3 Reading** (for each new P) | | | | |\n| 3a | `reader` | Paper, protocol 1.4–1.5 | Draft record: five Cs, Q scores, extraction fields, concepts, all with pages | — |\n| 3b | `citation-checker` | 3a + paper | Page references verified or flagged | — |\n| 3c | Me | 3a + 3b | Corrected record; key papers read in full | **Record accepted** |\n| **SLS 4 Synthesis** | | | | |\n| 4a | `synthesizer` | Accepted records | Proposed concepts, updated matrix, comparison for each concept | — |\n| 4b | Me | 4a | Concepts merged or split, comparisons accepted | **Matrix accepted** |\n| ↺ | `just check` | 2d | Did the round add new papers? Yes → back to 2c. No → 5a | Stop rule [1] |\n| **SLS 5 Gap** | | | | |\n| 5a | `synthesizer` | Final matrix | Draft SQ answers, gap, current solutions, history, limitations | — |\n| 5b | `skeptic` | 5a | Attacks the gap: really uncovered, or just not found? | — |\n| 5c | Me | 5a + 5b | Gap stated | **Gap** |\n| **DSRM 1 Problem (revision)** | | | | |\n| 6a | `synthesizer` | SLS 5, step 0 | Diff of step 0, claim by claim: confirmed / to revise / contradicted | — |\n| 6b | `skeptic` | Step 0 + 6a | Attacks motivation, H1–H3, and whether each RQ can be answered \"no\" | — |\n| 6c | Me | 6a + 6b | Revised `dsrm/1`, *provisional* removed | **Problem and RQs** |\n| **DSRM 2 Objectives** | | | | |\n| 7a | `skeptic` | RQs, SLS 5, my draft objectives | Each O checked: traces to an RQ, checkable, feasible | — |\n| 7b | Me | 7a | Objectives, metrics, baselines for RQ3 | **Objectives frozen** before any results |\n| **DSRM 3 Design** | | | | |\n| 8a | `designer` | Objectives, SLS 4, decisions so far | Options for each open decision, with trade-offs and prior art | — |\n| 8b | Me | 8a | Chosen option and reason, in the decisions table | **Design choices** |\n| 8c | `builder` | Decisions, current layer | Layer in its form and its checks | — |\n| 8d | Me | 8c | Layer reviewed; I can explain it | **Layer accepted** |\n| **DSRM 4 Demonstration** | | | | |\n| 9a | `demonstrator` | Layer, objectives | Proposed demonstration plan (D IDs, instances) | — |\n| 9b | Me | 9a | Plan approved | **Plan** |\n| 9c | `demonstrator` | Plan, layer | Runs or hand traces, D log entries | — |\n| 9d | Me | 9c | \"Solved\" confirmed | **Solved?** |\n| **DSRM 5 Evaluation** | | | | |\n| 10a | `evaluator` | Objectives, D log, metrics | Measurements against baselines, draft E entries, draft threats to validity | — |\n| 10b | `skeptic` | 10a | Attacks baselines, validity, choice of instances | — |\n| 10c | Me | 10a + 10b | Met / not met, threats addressed | **Results** |\n| ↺ | Me | 10c | Next layer or fix → 8a. Objective wrong → 7a. All objectives met → 11a | **Iteration** [2] |\n| **DSRM 6 Communicate** | | | | |\n| 11a | Me | Stable steps | Outline and key claims for each chapter | **Argument** |\n| 11b | `drafter` | 11a + sources | Chapter prose | — |\n| 11c | `citation-checker` | 11b | Each cited claim verified against its source | — |\n| 11d | `examiner` | 11b | Questions the committee would ask | — |\n| 11e | Me | 11b–11d | Final wording, contribution type, answers to the questions | **Text** |\n| ↺ | Me | 11d–11e | Writing exposes a hole → 7a or 8a | **Iteration** [2] |\n\n## Throughout\n- **`just check`** runs after every gate: traceability, the ID rule, stale chapters.\n- **AI log:** every agent step appends agent, step, what it proposed, and whether I accepted, changed or rejected it.\n\n---\n\n## References\n1. Wohlin (2014). *Guidelines for Snowballing in Systematic Literature Studies*. Conference on Evaluation and Assessment in Software Engineering.\n2. Peffers et al. (2007). *A Design Science Research Methodology for Information Systems Research*. Journal of Management Information Systems 24(3).\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b4aeb553-b9c8-4d8f-a6b8-d094d3c6e193","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
