{"parentUuid":"a2f1cc39-a1e7-4ae6-8031-445983f04c20","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm2ZDnzhLzg35NEb1iRB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've updated `research/agents.md` with all three changes. Nothing is committed.\n\n**1. Skills (new section).**\n- The top skill, `thesis`, asks for the entry point and then calls `sls` and `dsrm` in the order that entry point needs.\n- `sls` and `dsrm` each run their own steps and loops, through one skill per step (`sls-1-protocol` … `dsrm-6-communicate`).\n- Every skill can be called on its own; for example, `sls-3-reading P12` reads one paper.\n- Each section heading in the Flow table now names the skill that runs it.\n\n**2. Entry points (new section).** These are Peffers' four entry points, each with its route through the SLS and DSRM:\n- Problem-centred initiation: starts at DSRM 1. This is your thesis, and the Flow table is its route.\n- Objective-centred solution: starts at DSRM 2.\n- Design and development-centred initiation: starts at DSRM 3.\n- Client/context initiated: starts at DSRM 4, then works backward through 3, 2 and 1.\n\nA short list marks which rules are mine and not Peffers'.\n\n**3. AI log (rewritten section).** It now records everything, in two parts:\n- **Raw log:** Claude Code hooks write every prompt, skill call, agent start and stop, and every tool call with its full input and output. The session transcript is copied in at the end, because it holds the model's own messages, which hooks don't see. The agents don't write this log, so none of them can skip an entry.\n- **Decision log:** one entry per gate, pointing to the raw entries behind it.\n\n`just check` now also checks that every gate has a decision entry.\n\n**Please check before relying on it:** I wrote the entry-point names, their starting activities and the \"work backward … retroactively\" phrase for the client/context entry from memory of Peffers et al. (2007). Check them against the paper's process model figure and its text on entry points before you cite them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7304,"cache_read_input_tokens":70157,"output_tokens":682,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":46},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7304,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":682,"cache_read_input_tokens":70157,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7304},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"eea2b3b2-375d-4ed2-a552-3797b8b4c097","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfm2ZDRfmmso74GSVnC2q","type":"assistant","uuid":"693a1869-636c-413b-a5c1-3bc279554a31","timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:02:05.082Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
