{"parentUuid":"62874c34-97c7-44ef-a8b6-e607cd291398","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm3KoUm1fJ5xpEwSTuTy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bfq534BYbk4XS15kthew2D","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/README.md","content":"# AI workflow\n\nHow AI skills and agents run the steps of `sls/` and `dsrm/`. These are working rules. They do not change either method.\n\n## The line\n- **AI does the labour:** searching, drafting, building, measuring, writing prose.\n- **I make the decisions:** every gate in the flow. Each one is a decision, not a piece of work.\n- **Test:** I can defend every output at the defense with no AI in the room.\n- **Everything is logged:** every action the AI takes, not only the decisions (`ai-log.md`). The thesis Method chapter states how AI was used.\n\n## Files\n| File | Answers |\n|---|---|\n| `skills.md` | Which skills exist and how they call each other |\n| `agents.md` | Which agents exist and what each one does |\n| `entry-points.md` | Where the work can start, and the route from each start |\n| `kickstart.md` | Step 0, and the safeguards against my own bias |\n| `files.md` | How every output is stored: small files, one per output |\n| `flow-sls.md` | Rows 1a–5c: who reads and writes what, and where I decide |\n| `flow-dsrm.md` | Rows 6a–11e: same, for DSRM |\n| `ai-log.md` | How everything the AI does is recorded |\n| `checks.md` | What `just check` and `just views` do |\n\n## Order (problem-centred route)\nStep 0 (`kickstart.md`) → `flow-sls.md` → `flow-dsrm.md`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_read_input_tokens":91017,"output_tokens":8241,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":