{"parentUuid":"42b2f119-1d01-4acc-abc2-27580981177b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm3KoUm1fJ5xpEwSTuTy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018TzkHB6J6eXvnMnAgfmV6K","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/agents.md","content":"# Agents\n\nWorkers called by the step skills (`skills.md`). Each one proposes; I decide at the gate.\n\n| Agent | Used in | Does |\n|---|---|---|\n| `protocol-critic` | SLS 1 | Drafts the protocol from step 0; checks that SQs are answerable, criteria can be applied without ambiguity, and the form covers every SQ |\n| `snowballer` | SLS 2 | Proposes the search string and start set; fetches backward and forward candidates; pre-screens each against I/X |\n| `reader` | SLS 3 | Drafts the record for each paper: five Cs, Q scores, extraction fields, concepts, with pages |\n| `synthesizer` | SLS 4, SLS 5, DSRM 1 | Proposes concepts; drafts SQ answers and gap; compares SLS 5 against step 0 |\n| `designer` | DSRM 3 | For each open decision: options, trade-offs against objectives and prior art; critiques my proposals |\n| `builder` | DSRM 3 | Produces the current layer in its form (below) |\n| `demonstrator` | DSRM 4 | Proposes demonstrations; writes problem instances; runs or traces them |\n| `evaluator` | DSRM 5 | Measures against baselines; drafts evaluations and threats to validity |\n| `drafter` | DSRM 6 | Turns my outline and claims into section prose |\n| `examiner` | DSRM 6 | Plays the committee: asks the questions I will face at the defense |\n| `skeptic` | Any step | Looks for counter-evidence and attacks claims, gaps, objectives and results |\n| `citation-checker` | Any step | Checks that each cited claim appears in the source at the cited page |\n\n## Builder output per layer\nLayers from `dsrm/3-design/step.md`. The layer itself lives outside `research/`, in `artifact/L<n>/`; `dsrm/3-design/L<n>.md` describes it.\n\n| Layer | Form | Check |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Paper design | Spec document: instruction set, message format, actor lifecycle, diagrams | Consistency review, worked traces by hand |\n| 2. Executable model / simulator | Code and tests | Test suite, actor programs run end to end |\n| 3. Formal specification | TLA+ / Alloy / Coq model | Model checker or proof |\n| 4. Hardware prototype | HDL (Verilog / VHDL / Chisel), FPGA build | HDL simulation, synthesis reports, board runs |\n\nBesides the layers themselves, the builder also produces benchmark programs, the toolchain (assembler, language front end) and figures.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_read_input_tokens":91017,"output_tokens":8241,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8241,"cache_read_input_tokens":91017,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018TzkHB6J6eXvnMnAgfmV6K":{"file_path":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/agents.md","content":"# Agents\n\nWorkers called by the step skills (`skills.md`). Each one proposes; I decide at the gate.\n\n| Agent | Used in | Does |\n|---|---|---|\n| `protocol-critic` | SLS 1 | Drafts the protocol from step 0; checks that SQs are answerable, criteria can be applied without ambiguity, and the form covers every SQ |\n| `snowballer` | SLS 2 | Proposes the search string and start set; fetches backward and forward candidates; pre-screens each against I/X |\n| `reader` | SLS 3 | Drafts the record for each paper: five Cs, Q scores, extraction fields, concepts, with pages |\n| `synthesizer` | SLS 4, SLS 5, DSRM 1 | Proposes concepts; drafts SQ answers and gap; compares SLS 5 against step 0 |\n| `designer` | DSRM 3 | For each open decision: options, trade-offs against objectives and prior art; critiques my proposals |\n| `builder` | DSRM 3 | Produces the current layer in its form (below) |\n| `demonstrator` | DSRM 4 | Proposes demonstrations; writes problem instances; runs or traces them |\n| `evaluator` | DSRM 5 | Measures against baselines; drafts evaluations and threats to validity |\n| `drafter` | DSRM 6 | Turns my outline and claims into section prose |\n| `examiner` | DSRM 6 | Plays the committee: asks the questions I will face at the defense |\n| `skeptic` | Any step | Looks for counter-evidence and attacks claims, gaps, objectives and results |\n| `citation-checker` | Any step | Checks that each cited claim appears in the source at the cited page |\n\n## Builder output per layer\nLayers from `dsrm/3-design/step.md`. The layer itself lives outside `research/`, in `artifact/L<n>/`; `dsrm/3-design/L<n>.md` describes it.\n\n| Layer | Form | Check |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Paper design | Spec document: instruction set, message format, actor lifecycle, diagrams | Consistency review, worked traces by hand |\n| 2. Executable model / simulator | Code and tests | Test suite, actor programs run end to end |\n| 3. Formal specification | TLA+ / Alloy / Coq model | Model checker or proof |\n| 4. Hardware prototype | HDL (Verilog / VHDL / Chisel), FPGA build | HDL simulation, synthesis reports, board runs |\n\nBesides the layers themselves, the builder also produces benchmark programs, the toolchain (assembler, language front end) and figures.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"91cb8e6b-fc61-4f07-8817-d0195893af28","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cfm3Ko9QsWkD4WN9EycNH","type":"assistant","uuid":"877e52cb-aa6b-485e-afda-de7854a68a80","timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:12:17.922Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"877e52cb-aa6b-485e-afda-de7854a68a80","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm3KoUm1fJ5xpEwSTuTy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VyLgLRrp2fsqTDVNcscbk9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/entry-points.md","content":"# Entry points\n\nPeffers et al. define four entry points [1]. The DSRM sequence is the same in all four; only the starting activity changes. The `thesis` skill asks for one (`skills.md`).\n\n| Entry point [1] | Starts at | Trigger | Route |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Problem-centred initiation | DSRM 1 | An observed problem | Step 0 (my `dsrm/1` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 revised → 2 → 3–5 loop → 6. **This thesis.** `flow-sls.md` and `flow-dsrm.md` are this route. |\n| Objective-centred solution | DSRM 2 | A need that a better artifact could meet | Step 0 (my `dsrm/2` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 written, 2 revised → 3–5 loop → 6 |\n| Design and development-centred initiation | DSRM 3 | An existing artifact not yet thought through as a solution to this problem | Step 0 (the artifact, described in `dsrm/3`) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1–2 written for the problem it solves → 3–5 loop → 6 |\n| Client/context initiated | DSRM 4 | A practical solution observed to work | Step 0 (the observed solution, in `dsrm/4`) → SLS 1–5 → work backward through DSRM 3, 2, 1 to apply rigor retroactively [1] → 5 → 6 |\n\nMy rules for all four (not part of Peffers):\n- Step 0 is always my draft of the starting activity, with status `provisional` (`kickstart.md`).\n- The SLS always runs right after step 0, because DSRM 1–3 need it (`research/README.md`).\n- The kickstart safeguards apply whatever the entry point.\n\n---\n\n## References\n1. Peffers et al. (2007). *A Design Science Research Methodology for Information Systems Research*. Journal of Management Information Systems 24(3).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_read_input_tokens":91017,"output_tokens":8241,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8241,"cache_read_input_tokens":91017,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VyLgLRrp2fsqTDVNcscbk9":{"file_path":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/entry-points.md","content":"# Entry points\n\nPeffers et al. define four entry points [1]. The DSRM sequence is the same in all four; only the starting activity changes. The `thesis` skill asks for one (`skills.md`).\n\n| Entry point [1] | Starts at | Trigger | Route |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Problem-centred initiation | DSRM 1 | An observed problem | Step 0 (my `dsrm/1` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 revised → 2 → 3–5 loop → 6. **This thesis.** `flow-sls.md` and `flow-dsrm.md` are this route. |\n| Objective-centred solution | DSRM 2 | A need that a better artifact could meet | Step 0 (my `dsrm/2` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 written, 2 revised → 3–5 loop → 6 |\n| Design and development-centred initiation | DSRM 3 | An existing artifact not yet thought through as a solution to this problem | Step 0 (the artifact, described in `dsrm/3`) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1–2 written for the problem it solves → 3–5 loop → 6 |\n| Client/context initiated | DSRM 4 | A practical solution observed to work | Step 0 (the observed solution, in `dsrm/4`) → SLS 1–5 → work backward through DSRM 3, 2, 1 to apply rigor retroactively [1] → 5 → 6 |\n\nMy rules for all four (not part of Peffers):\n- Step 0 is always my draft of the starting activity, with status `provisional` (`kickstart.md`).\n- The SLS always runs right after step 0, because DSRM 1–3 need it (`research/README.md`).\n- The kickstart safeguards apply whatever the entry point.\n\n---\n\n## References\n1. Peffers et al. (2007). *A Design Science Research Methodology for Information Systems Research*. Journal of Management Information Systems 24(3).\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"91cb8e6b-fc61-4f07-8817-d0195893af28","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cfm3Ko9QsWkD4WN9EycNH","type":"assistant","uuid":"48b17d2b-a662-4355-bf4b-896fab372d86","timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:12:22.831Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"48b17d2b-a662-4355-bf4b-896fab372d86","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm3KoUm1fJ5xpEwSTuTy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Jw44V13PJDWyHdq7chNJWH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/kickstart.md","content":"# Kickstart\n\nThe pipeline starts from my provisional draft: step 0. For the problem-centred route (`entry-points.md`):\n\n| # | Who | Input | Output | Gate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **0** | Me | — | `dsrm/1-problem/`: `observation.md`, `motivation.md`, `H{n}.md`, `stakeholders.md`, `design-problem.md`, `RQ{n}.md`, all `provisional` | — |\n\n## Safeguards\nThat draft already argues for a conclusion, so:\n- **Protocol bias:** SQs drawn only from my hypotheses would only look for support. `skeptic` adds SQs that look for evidence against them (row 1b, `flow-sls.md`).\n- **Start set bias:** snowballing only from my own references mostly finds more of the same. The start set also uses a database search string (row 2a), as Wohlin recommends a varied start set [1].\n\n## Closing the loop\nAt the end of the SLS, the loop returns to step 0: the `synthesizer` lists which claims are confirmed, need revising or are contradicted (row 6a, `flow-dsrm.md`), and I revise the draft before setting it to `accepted`.\n\n---\n\n## References\n1. Wohlin (2014). *Guidelines for Snowballing in Systematic Literature Studies*. Conference on Evaluation and Assessment in Software Engineering.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_read_input_tokens":91017,"output_tokens":8241,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inferenc