{"parentUuid":"48b17d2b-a662-4355-bf4b-896fab372d86","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2419a529-f839-4a01-8c3d-f915f75e005c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VyLgLRrp2fsqTDVNcscbk9","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/entry-points.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"5095e6e4-148d-4038-8a1c-acceea8bcadc","timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:12:58.048Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/entry-points.md","content":"# Entry points\n\nPeffers et al. define four entry points [1]. The DSRM sequence is the same in all four; only the starting activity changes. The `thesis` skill asks for one (`skills.md`).\n\n| Entry point [1] | Starts at | Trigger | Route |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Problem-centred initiation | DSRM 1 | An observed problem | Step 0 (my `dsrm/1` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 revised → 2 → 3–5 loop → 6. **This thesis.** `flow-sls.md` and `flow-dsrm.md` are this route. |\n| Objective-centred solution | DSRM 2 | A need that a better artifact could meet | Step 0 (my `dsrm/2` draft) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1 written, 2 revised → 3–5 loop → 6 |\n| Design and development-centred initiation | DSRM 3 | An existing artifact not yet thought through as a solution to this problem | Step 0 (the artifact, described in `dsrm/3`) → SLS 1–5 → DSRM 1–2 written for the problem it solves → 3–5 loop → 6 |\n| Client/context initiated | DSRM 4 | A practical solution observed to work | Step 0 (the observed solution, in `dsrm/4`) → SLS 1–5 → work backward through DSRM 3, 2, 1 to apply rigor retroactively [1] → 5 → 6 |\n\nMy rules for all four (not part of Peffers):\n- Step 0 is always my draft of the starting activity, with status `provisional` (`kickstart.md`).\n- The SLS always runs right after step 0, because DSRM 1–3 need it (`research/README.md`).\n- The kickstart safeguards apply whatever the entry point.\n\n---\n\n## References\n1. Peffers et al. (2007). *A Design Science Research Methodology for Information Systems Research*. Journal of Management Information Systems 24(3).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"48b17d2b-a662-4355-bf4b-896fab372d86","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
