{"parentUuid":"29a9671e-4007-430e-8cd3-1716d2cd313d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm3dskjL5Nu6n4bXokHB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, I think it's worth it, as long as the template **replaces** the spec part of each `step.md` rather than duplicating it. Two descriptions of the same file always drift apart.\n\n**What it gives you:**\n1. **One source of truth for file shapes.** Agents write their output by filling the template, so the file has the same sections and frontmatter every time.\n2. **Checks become possible.** `just check` can compare each produced file with its template: missing sections, missing frontmatter keys, leftover placeholders. Right now \"complete when written\" is only a promise.\n3. **A new project starts by copying it.** That matters for the entry points: an objective-centred project copies the same tree and starts at `dsrm/2`.\n4. **You can see the whole pipeline in one tree,** which is also the clearest way to show your advisor the method.\n\n**Where it should live:** at `research/template/`, not inside `ai/`. The file shapes belong to the method, not to the AI. You'd fill the same templates by hand.\n\n**What it would look like** (it mirrors `research/`, with one template per kind of file):\n```\nresearch/template/\n├── dsrm/\n│   ├── 1-problem/      observation.md  motivation.md  H.md  stakeholders.md\n│   │                   design-problem.md  RQ.md  revision.md\n│   ├── 2-objectives/   O.md  metrics.md  baselines.md\n│   ├── 3-design/       DEC.options.md  DEC.md  L.md\n│   ├── 4-demonstration/ D.md  D-run.md\n│   ├── 5-evaluation/   E.md  T.md\n│   └── 6-communicate/  section.outline.md  section.draft.md  contribution.md\n├── sls/\n│   ├── 1-protocol/     need.md  SQ.md  criteria.md  quality.md  extraction-form.md  change.md\n│   ├── 2-search/       search-string.md  R.md\n│   ├── 3-reading/      P.md\n│   ├── 4-synthesis/    C.md\n│   └── 5-gap/          SQ.answer.md  gap.md  solutions.md  history.md  limitations.md\n├── reviews/            skeptic.md  citations.md  examiner.md\n└── ai-log/             decision.md\n```\nEach template holds the frontmatter, the section headings, and a `{placeholder}` with a one-line instruction for each field. Templates are the only files allowed to contain placeholders.\n\n**What changes elsewhere:**\n- `step.md` shrinks to the method itself: what the step means, its sources, its rules. It points to its templates instead of containing forms.\n- `faq.md` stays as it is.\n- In `ai/files.md`, \"`step.md` becomes the spec\" becomes \"the template is the spec\".\n- In the flow tables, each output names the template it fills.\n\nShould I build it? The order I'd use: write the templates first, shrink the `step.md` files, then migrate your `dsrm/1` content into the new files. Your uncommitted changes to `dsrm/1-problem/step.md` are what makes the order matter. If you commit them first, I can split that file into the new files without risking your edits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63,"cache_read_input_tokens":101846,"output_tokens":1500,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":464},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1500,"cache_read_input_tokens":101846,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c773e342-8c79-4b28-808b-cd4b033cc351","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfm3ds2acUWzPPQWA5N5Y","type":"assistant","uuid":"82e6559a-aae