{"parentUuid":"6329bb90-eb8a-4fbe-b2fb-d8a6a9273e68","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm3rYdAL9Tx5vB2UB9GB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've separated step 0 from DSRM 1 in the `ai/` docs. Your `dsrm/1-problem/step.md` itself is untouched.\n\n**The split:**\n- **Step 0 is what you define**, in a new top-level folder, `research/0-start/`. It's frozen before the SLS starts and never edited afterwards; only its status changes.\n- **DSRM 1 is what's built with AI** from step 0 and the SLS, in `dsrm/1-problem/`. Nothing there overwrites step 0. If you revise something from step 0, the new version gets a new ID in `dsrm/1-problem/` and the old one is marked retired, which is your existing ID rule.\n\n**Where your current `dsrm/1-problem/step.md` content would go:**\n\n| Current section | Goes to | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1.1 Observation | `0-start/observation.md` | Your intent |\n| 1.1 \"Semantic gap (Myers)\" | `0-start/claims.md` | A claim about the literature, for the SLS to check |\n| 1.2 Why solving it matters | `0-start/claims.md` | Claims about the literature, for the SLS to check |\n| 1.2 Scope (deadlock, atomicity, ordering) | `0-start/stances.md` | Your design choices |\n| 1.2 Go counter-evidence | `0-start/claims.md` | A claim about the literature |\n| 1.2 Why earlier attempts failed (432, SOAR, J-Machine, Lisp machines) | `0-start/claims.md` | Claims about the literature |\n| 1.2 H1–H3 | `0-start/H1.md`, `H2.md`, `H3.md` | What you believe; RQ3 tests them |\n| 1.2 \"Which of these hold\" | removed | Answered later, in the `dsrm/5-evaluation/E*.md` files |\n| 1.3 Stakeholders | `0-start/stakeholders.md` | Your choice |\n| 1.4 Design problem | `0-start/design-problem.md` | What you want to solve |\n| 1.5 RQ3, RQ5 | `0-start/RQ3.md`, `RQ5.md` | What you want to find out |\n| 1.5 Metrics, baselines `[ ]` | `dsrm/2-objectives/metrics.md`, `baselines.md` | Belong to objectives, not to the problem |\n| References 4–21 | `0-start/seeds.md` | Seeds for the start set, not results |\n\n**What DSRM 1 now builds** (rows 6a–6d in `flow-dsrm.md`):\n- `revision.md`: each claim in `claims.md` marked confirmed, to revise, or contradicted, with the papers that show it.\n- `problem.skeptic.md`: an attack on your intent files.\n- `motivation.md`: why it matters and why earlier attempts failed, backed by the reviewed papers.\n- New-ID versions of anything you choose to revise.\n\n**Other files updated:**\n- `kickstart.md`: lists what each `0-start/` file holds, and the rule that step 0 is never edited.\n- `flow-sls.md`: rows 1a, 1b and 2a now read from `0-start/`. Row 2a uses `seeds.md` for the start set.\n- `entry-points.md`: step 0 is `0-start/` for every entry point.\n\n**One thing to fix in your content:** RQ5's evidence column has an open list: \"`[ ]`: protection, scheduling, resource allocation?\". Which operating-system functions RQ5 covers is part of your question, so you need to settle it before step 0 is frozen.\n\nTo do the actual move, commit your changes to `dsrm/1-problem/step.md` first. Then I'll split that file into `0-start/` exactly as in the table above."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3893,"cache_read_input_tokens":114596,"output_tokens":1327,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":64},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3893,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1327,"cache_read_input_tokens":114596,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3893},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClass