{"parentUuid":"7949dc5b-8290-4da7-845e-c7de009164a5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/checks.md","snippet":"2\t\n3\tTwo `just` recipes. Neither is an agent: both are scripts, so they give the same answer every time.\n4\t\n5\t## `just check`\n6\tRuns after every gate. Fails if any of these is broken:\n7\t- **Traceability:** every file names IDs that exist (O → RQ, D → O, E → O and D).\n8\t- **ID rule:** no ID was renamed or removed; it was retired instead (`dsrm/README.md`).\n9\t- **Stale chapters:** a chapter section whose sources changed after it was accepted.\n10\t- **Complete files:** no `{placeholder}` or `[ ]` left, and every section of the template present (`files.md`).\n11\t- **Decisions:** every gate has a decision file (`ai-log.md`).\n12\t- **Stop rule:** reports whether the last snowballing round added new papers (`flow-sls.md`).\n13\t\n14\t## `just views`\n15\tRegenerates `views/` from frontmatter (`files.md`). Never edited by hand.\n16\t- Paper list\n17\t- Concept matrix\n18\t- Traceability: RQ → O → D → E"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d3d4c16c-880b-495e-8e00-881d6e22368a","timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:25:18.003Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/checks.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n2\t\n3\tTwo `just` recipes. Neither is an agent: both are scripts, so they give the same answer every time.\n4\t\n5\t## `just check`\n6\tRuns after every gate. Fails if any of these is broken:\n7\t- **Traceability:** every file names IDs that exist (O → RQ, D → O, E → O and D).\n8\t- **ID rule:** no ID was renamed or removed; it was retired instead (`dsrm/README.md`).\n9\t- **Stale chapters:** a chapter section whose sources changed after it was accepted.\n10\t- **Complete files:** no `{placeholder}` or `[ ]` left, and every section of the template present (`files.md`).\n11\t- **Decisions:** every gate has a decision file (`ai-log.md`).\n12\t- **Stop rule:** reports whether the last snowballing round added new papers (`flow-sls.md`).\n13\t\n14\t## `just views`\n15\tRegenerates `views/` from frontmatter (`files.md`). Never edited by hand.\n16\t- Paper list\n17\t- Concept matrix\n18\t- Traceability: RQ → O → D → E\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d3d4c16c-880b-495e-8e00-881d6e22368a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/files.md","snippet":"1\t# Files\n2\t\n3\tSmall files, each produced whole in one transaction. No large file that fills up over months.\n4\t\n5\t## Rules\n6\t- **One file per output.** Each flow row writes the exact files listed in its Output column, and reads only the files in its Input column (`flow-sls.md`, `flow-dsrm.md`).\n7\t- **One file per entity,** named by its ID: `SQ1.md`, `P12.md`, `C3.md`, `O1.md`, `D1.md`, `E1.md`. Anything that would grow (a log, a list of rounds) is a folder of entries instead.\n8\t- **Reviews of a file sit next to it,** named `<file>.<kind>.md`: `P12.citations.md`, `gap.skeptic.md`.\n9\t- **Complete when written.** A file has no `{placeholder}` or `[ ]` left. If a field cannot be filled, it says why.\n10\t- **A gate changes only `status`.** If I change content, the decision file says what and why (`ai-log.md`).\n11\t- **Tables are generated, not written.** The concept matrix, paper list, traceability (RQ → O → D → E) and chapter status are built by `just views` into `views/`, which is never edited by hand (`checks.md`).\n12\t- **The template is the spec.** Every file is a copy of its template in `research/template/`, which lists where each one is saved and which row writes it. `step.md` keeps only the method: what the step means, its sources, its rules. `faq.md` stays as it is.\n13\t\n14\t## Frontmatter\n15\tOn every file:\n16\t```\n17\t---\n18\tid: P12\n19\trow: 3a                    # the flow row that wrote it\n20\tby: reader                 # agent name, or me"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fdb7293a-5268-4b04-859f-f66c2370fcba","timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:25:18.004Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research/ai/files.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t# Files\n2\t\n3\tSmall files, each produced whole in one transaction. No large file that fills up over months.\n4\t\n5\t## Rules\n6\t- **One file per output.** Each flow row writes the exact files listed in its Output column, and reads only the files in its Input column (`flow-sls.md`, `flow-dsrm.md`).\n7\t- **One file per entity,** named by its ID: `SQ1.md`, `P12.md`, `C3.md`, `O1.md`, `D1.md`, `E1.md`. Anything that would grow (a log, a list of rounds) is a folder of entries instead.\n8\t- **Reviews of a file sit next to it,** named `<file>.<kind>.md`: `P12.citations.md`, `gap.skeptic.md`.\n9\t- **Complete when written.** A file has no `{placeholder}` or `[ ]` left. If a field cannot be filled, it says why.\n10\t- **A gate changes only `status`.** If I change content, the decision file says what and why (`ai-log.md`).\n11\t- **Tables are generated, not written.** The concept matrix, paper list, traceability (RQ → O → D → E) and chapter status are built by `just views` into `views/`, which is never edited by hand (`checks.md`).\n12\t- **The template is the spec.** Every file is a copy of its template in `research/template/`, which lists where each one is saved and which row writes it. `step.md` keeps only the method: what the step means, its sources, its rules. `faq.md` stays as it is.\n13\t\n14\t## Frontmatter\n15\tOn every file:\n16\t```\n17\t---\n18\tid: P12\n19\trow: 3a                    # the flow row that wrote it\n20\tby: reader                 # agent name, or me\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/garro/dev/faculty/Thesis/research","sessionId":"f5479a1a-28cc-4c2d-bc70-ca6abee30b5e","version":"2.1.289","gitBranch":"main"}
