{"parentUuid":"fef4aafc-5804-4b66-b3a9-16e58dfe1bea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm5bD31KbcYs7tTJVmfT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built 14 skills and 12 agents from the `ai/` docs. Nothing is committed, and I haven't run any of them yet.\n\n**Agents** (`.claude/agents/`): one file per agent in `ai/agents.md`. Each file holds only that agent's role and its tools. For example, `snowballer` can search the web and query OpenAlex or Semantic Scholar with `curl`, and `builder` can edit files and run commands.\n\n**Skills** (`.claude/skills/`):\n- **Facades:** `/thesis`, `/sls` and `/dsrm`. A facade reaches the step skills by reading their `SKILL.md` files.\n- **Step skills:** `/sls-1-protocol` … `/sls-5-gap` and `/dsrm-1-problem` … `/dsrm-6-communicate`.\n- **Arguments:** a few step skills take one. `/sls-3-reading P12` reads one paper, `/dsrm-3-design decide <topic>` or `/dsrm-3-design build` picks a path, `/dsrm-6-communicate ch1-intro` works on one section, and `/sls-1-protocol change` records a protocol change.\n- **User-invoked only:** every skill runs only when you type it, so none adds anything to my context until called.\n\n**Three new shared procedures in `ai/`**, so each rule is written once:\n- **`agent-contract.md`:** what every agent receives, the template-filling rules, when its output counts as done, and what it reports back. Agents must not use any fact they can't trace to a source they read in that run.\n- **`running.md`:** how a skill runs a row, and how it resumes from the first row the files show isn't done. It also covers rows you do yourself (7a, 8b, 11a, 11e), where the skill writes files from your words only.\n- **`gate.md`:** present each file with its review flags, wait for your decision, apply it, write the decision file, then run `just check`.\n\n**Decisions I made that you should check:**\n- `/sls-1-protocol` starts with a gate for row 0: you accept the `0-start/` files, which freezes step 0. It won't draft the protocol until `observation.md` is accepted.\n- `/thesis` asks for the entry point, but only problem-centred initiation has rows defined. For the other three, it says so and stops.\n\n**Still missing:**\n1. **`.claude/` is ignored by git.** Your `.gitignore` starts with `.*`, so none of these skills or agents would be versioned. Since they're part of your method and of your AI-use disclosure, I'd add `!.claude/` to `.gitignore`. Tell me if I should.\n2. **`just check` and `just views` don't exist yet.** The skills say so and carry on without them.\n3. **The raw-log hooks aren't set up.** Until they are, decision files say \"raw log not set up\", so the \"log everything\" rule isn't in force yet.\n\nSkills and agents in `.claude/` are usually picked up only when a session starts, so restart the session before trying `/sls-1-protocol` as the first real run."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":201054,"output_tokens":1088,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":86},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1088,"cache_read_input_tokens":201054,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2dc8109c-c135-4664-b83e-023f1cfaff37","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfm5bChuSUz9qkWHv9rcr","attributionSkill":"mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents","attributionPlugin":"mattpocock-skills","type":"assistant","uuid":"cfbcfe16-8aad-4998-9be2-1b9702b8d