{"parentUuid":"4022397c-5c18-4cbb-b62d-570e9b77d291","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm5xEnGVSMoB1yU1dbez","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've done all three, and the hooks are already live: they're logging this session.\n\n**`just check` and `just views`** both run one script, `ai/tools/research.py`, which uses only the Python standard library.\n- **`just check`** fails on any of these:\n  - a status that isn't one of the six allowed values\n  - a file with no matching template, a missing template section, or a leftover `{placeholder}` / `[ ]`\n  - a decided file with no decision file\n  - an ID removed or renamed since the last commit\n  - a broken link between IDs (O→RQ, H→RQ, D→O/L, E→RQ/O/runs, L→DEC)\n  - a stale chapter section\n\n  It also reports where the snowballing stop rule stands.\n- **`just views`** writes four files to `research/views/`: the paper list, the concept matrix, the traceability chain (RQ → O → D → runs → E) and chapter status.\n- **Tested:** your real files pass. On a fake research tree with seven errors planted on purpose, it caught all seven, and the views came out right.\n- **`ai/checks.md`** now describes each rule exactly as the script implements it.\n\n**`.claude/` is now tracked by git.** `.claude/settings.local.json` stays ignored, since it's personal.\n\n**Raw-log hooks:**\n- `.claude/settings.json` sends every hook event (session start and end, your prompts, tool calls before and after, agent stops, compaction) to `ai/tools/log_hook.py`.\n- That script appends each event to `research/ai-log/raw/<session>.jsonl` and keeps a copy of the full transcript next to it.\n- At session start it gives the model the session ID, which gates now write into decision files.\n- If anything goes wrong it fails silently, so it can never block a session.\n- **It's working:** this session's log already has entries.\n\n**Privacy:** the raw log is tracked by git and holds everything you type and every tool output. Keep that in mind before pushing the repo anywhere public.\n\nNothing is committed yet.\n\n## How to do a full run\n\n1. **Finish step 0.** Fill in \"How I noticed it\" in `research/0-start/observation.md`. If you want, settle the open RQ5 marker in `notes.md`.\n2. **Restart Claude Code** in this repo, so the skills and hooks load cleanly.\n3. **Run `/thesis`** and pick *Problem-centred initiation*.\n\nIt then goes through `/sls` and `/dsrm` on its own and stops at every gate for your decision. A full run won't finish in one session: snowballing alone takes several rounds. Just run `/thesis` again in any later session and it resumes from the first row the files show isn't done.\n\nYou can also run parts of it directly:\n- a whole method: `/sls`, `/dsrm`\n- one step: `/sls-3-reading`, `/dsrm-3-design build`\n- one paper: `/sls-3-reading P12`\n\n**One gap to fix before reading starts:** `reader` can't get full text for paywalled papers, and the workflow doesn't yet say where to put PDFs you download yourself. I'd add a `research/papers/P{n}.pdf` folder that `reader` checks first. Want me to add it, and commit all of this?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":481,"cache_read_input_tokens":225964,"output_tokens":1448,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":389},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":481,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1448,"cache_read_input_tokens":225964,"cache_creation_input_tokens":481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":481},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fd07