{"parentUuid":"e2f52c9f-6323-4e2d-8d7a-d90c79ee62af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfm6JabCEd4uo8qCNJT3n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've set up `research/papers/` and publishing to GitHub. I haven't run any `gh` command, so the publishing part is untested. Nothing is committed.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Local folder:** `research/papers/` holds one PDF per included paper, named `P{n}.pdf`. Its `README.md` is tracked by git, but the PDFs are ignored, which keeps the history small.\n- **Where the PDFs come from:**\n  - You drop in the ones you get yourself.\n  - `reader` saves every PDF it reaches online on its own.\n- **Where `reader` reads from, in order:**\n  1. `research/papers/P{n}.pdf`\n  2. the full text online, downloading it into the folder when it's a PDF\n  3. the abstract only, which it notes in the record\n\n  `citation-checker` also checks the folder first.\n- **Publishing:**\n  - `just papers-push` uploads every PDF in the folder to a GitHub release named `papers`, creating the release the first time and replacing files that are already there.\n  - `just papers-pull` downloads them, for example on another machine.\n- **Automatic in `/sls-3-reading`:** it pulls before reading and pushes after the gate, so every accepted paper's PDF gets published.\n\nI also updated row 3a in `ai/flow-sls.md` and the folder table in `research/README.md`.\n\n**Check before the first push:** release assets have the same visibility as the repo. If your thesis repo is public, anyone can download those PDFs. For papers you got through the library or behind a paywall, that's redistributing copyrighted work. If the repo is public, either make it private or only add open-access PDFs to the folder.\n\n`just papers-push` needs the `gh` CLI logged in. To test it yourself, drop any PDF into `research/papers/` and run `! just papers-push`.\n\nWant me to commit everything from this round: the checks, vie